Source: am5-spd-diag
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Fritz <code@fritztech.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 13), make, rustc, cargo, libgtk-4-dev, pkg-config, python3, systemd, zstd, xz-utils
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/fritz-fritz/am5-spd-diag
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: am5-spd-diag
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, systemd
Recommends: dmidecode, i2c-tools, pkexec | policykit-1
Description: AM5 DDR5 SPD hub diagnostics after sleep/warm reboot
 Capture DIMM/SPD identity across boot, shutdown, and systemd sleep/resume
 on AMD AM5 systems. Helps document the AGESA/firmware failure where a
 warm reboot after sleep reports Unknown/2 GiB DIMMs until AC power is
 removed.
 .
 Optional tools: dmidecode (SMBIOS fallback), i2c-tools (SPD5118 hub
 probe/recover), and pkexec (graphical snapshot for report/package).
 Notification clicks open the in-app GTK results window.
